# cloak/travel_front: the travel cloak over the shoulders: two shoulder drapes and a leather cord to a brass clasp at the throat.
# Rigid (its own channel, so it never vanishes on a frame's hang key): facing down it lies over the shoulders above the
# arms (the head layer, under the head); facing right and left it wraps the near shoulder; facing up the panel (drawn
# after, in cloakFront) covers the shoulder caps it keeps there. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) under T4 plate (cloak.t3,armour.t4) only the cord and the clasp: the steel pauldrons read.
use person
body adult
role cloak travel
layer neck
anchor neck
keys cloakfront
z 2
legend Q cloak 0
legend R cloak 1
legend S cloak 2
legend T cloak 3
legend U cloak 4

view U key rest origin 9 0 layer head
|..QQQQ......QQQQ..
|.QTTSQ......QSSRQ.

view D key rest origin 9 0 layer head
|..QQQQ......QQQQ..
|.QTTSQggPOggQSSRQ.
|QTTSSQ......QSSRRQ
|QTTSQ........QSRRQ
|.QTQ..........QRQ.

view R key rest origin 7 1
|............
|..QQQ....PO.
|.QTSSQggg...
|.QTSSRQ.....
|.QTSSRQ.....
|.QTSRQ......
|.QTSRQ......
|.QTSRQ......
|.QTRQ.......
|..QQ........

view L key rest origin 4 1
|............
|.PO....QQQ..
|...iiiQSSSQ.
|.....QTSSSQ.
|.....QTSSSQ.
|......QTSSQ.
|......QTSSQ.
|......QTSSQ.
|.......QTSQ.
|........QQ..

view U key rest origin 9 0 layer head when cloak.t3,armour.t4 replace
|..................
|..................

